// Title: ESXi VM Kill Via ESXCLI
// Sigma ID: 2992ac4d-31e9-4325-99f2-b18a73221bb2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Cedric Maurugeon
// Date: 2023-09-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, impact, T1059.012, T1529
// Description: Detects execution of the "esxcli" command with the "vm" and "kill" flag in order to
//   kill/shutdown a specific VM.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/hypervisor-jackpotting-ecrime-actors-increase-targeting-of-esxi-servers/
//   - https://developer.broadcom.com/xapis/esxcli-command-reference/7.0.0/namespace/esxcli_vm.html
//   - https://www.secuinfra.com/en/techtalk/hide-your-hypervisor-analysis-of-esxiargs-ransomware/
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/22/e/new-linux-based-ransomware-cheerscrypt-targets-exsi-devices.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_esxcli_vm_kill.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/esxcli" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "vm process" and ProcessCommandLine contains "kill")
